IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sg-core`
IMPORT `sg-definitions`
IMPORT `sg-groups`
IMPORT `sga2-nouns`

-- Companies Act 1967 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition: s 76(8), (8A) and (9) -- what nothing in s 76(1) or (1A) prohibits.
-- Layer 1. One function per paragraph, each with its own conditions.
--
-- HOW THE EXCEPTIONS ANSWER. Each paragraph is a carve-out: "Nothing in subsection (1) or (1A) prohibits ...". A function named for it answers
--   JUST TRUE  when the facts bring the act within the paragraph (the subsections do not prohibit it);
--   NOTHING    when they do not: the paragraph then says nothing, and subsection (1) or (1A) decides by its own words. A failed gate is not a bar
--              (the grant rule of 2026-11-12, limit 1: a carve-out is a permission, and its failing must not read as "prohibited"); marker {F-A7}.
-- The paragraphs are a list the text does not close with "only", and are not exclusive of rules of law (s 76(8)(o)).
-- The borrowed Acts (Insolvency, Restructuring and Dissolution Act 2018) and the Orders of Court are facts the caller states.

§ `Section 76(8): the exceptions for lawful dealings`

-- (8)(a): a distribution of a company's assets by way of dividends lawfully made.
-- src:7436 | (8) Nothing in subsection (1) or (1A) prohibits —
-- src:7438 | (a) a distribution of a company’s assets by way of dividends
-- src:7439 | lawfully made;
@ref s 76(8)(a) (src:7436-7439)
GIVEN `the act is a distribution of the company's assets by way of dividends` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the dividends were lawfully made` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 76(8)(a) the act is one that subsections (1) and (1A) do not prohibit because it is a lawful dividend` MEANS
    IF `the act is a distribution of the company's assets by way of dividends` AND `the dividends were lawfully made`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Nothing in subsection (1) or (1A) prohibits (a) a distribution of a company's assets by way of dividends lawfully made" -- a failed gate does not make the act prohibited {F-A7}

-- (8)(aa): a distribution in the course of a company's winding up.
-- src:7436 | (8) Nothing in subsection (1) or (1A) prohibits —
-- src:7441 | (aa) a distribution in the course of a company’s winding up;
@ref s 76(8)(aa) (src:7436-7441)
GIVEN `the act is a distribution in the course of the company's winding up` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 76(8)(aa) the act is one that subsections (1) and (1A) do not prohibit because it is a distribution in a winding up` MEANS
    IF `the act is a distribution in the course of the company's winding up`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Nothing in subsection (1) or (1A) prohibits ... (aa) a distribution in the course of a company's winding up" {F-A7}

-- (8)(b): a payment made by a company pursuant to a reduction of capital in accordance with Division 3A of this Part (Part 4).
-- src:7436 | (8) Nothing in subsection (1) or (1A) prohibits —
-- src:7446 | (b) a payment made by a company pursuant to a reduction of
-- src:7447 | capital in accordance with Division 3A of this Part;
@ref s 76(8)(b) (src:7436-7447)
GIVEN `the act is a payment made by the company pursuant to a reduction of capital` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the reduction of capital is in accordance with Division 3A of Part 4` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 76(8)(b) the act is one that subsections (1) and (1A) do not prohibit because it is a payment on a reduction of capital` MEANS
    IF `the act is a payment made by the company pursuant to a reduction of capital` AND `the reduction of capital is in accordance with Division 3A of Part 4`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Nothing in subsection (1) or (1A) prohibits ... (b) a payment made by a company pursuant to a reduction of capital in accordance with Division 3A of this Part" {F-A7}

-- (8)(c): the discharge by a company of a liability of the company that was incurred in good faith as a result of a transaction entered into on ordinary commercial terms.
-- src:7436 | (8) Nothing in subsection (1) or (1A) prohibits —
-- src:7449 | (c) the discharge by a company of a liability of the company
-- src:7450 | that was incurred in good faith as a result of a transaction
-- src:7451 | entered into on ordinary commercial terms;
@ref s 76(8)(c) (src:7436-7451)
GIVEN `the act is the discharge by the company of a liability of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the liability was incurred in good faith` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the liability was incurred as a result of a transaction entered into on ordinary commercial terms` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 76(8)(c) the act is one that subsections (1) and (1A) do not prohibit because it is the discharge of a liability incurred in good faith` MEANS
    IF    `the act is the discharge by the company of a liability of the company`
      AND `the liability was incurred in good faith`
      AND `the liability was incurred as a result of a transaction entered into on ordinary commercial terms`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Nothing in subsection (1) or (1A) prohibits ... (c) the discharge by a company of a liability of the company that was incurred in good faith as a result of a transaction entered into on ordinary commercial terms" {F-A7}

