      `the act was done in the ordinary course of commercial dealing` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 76(8)(j) the act is one that subsections (1) and (1A) do not prohibit because it is an agreement for payment by instalments` MEANS
    IF    `the act is the entering into of an agreement by the company with a subscriber for shares in the company`
      AND `the agreement permits the subscriber to make payments for the shares by instalments`
      AND `the act was done in good faith`
      AND `the act was done in the ordinary course of commercial dealing`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Nothing in subsection (1) or (1A) prohibits ... (j) the entering into, in good faith and in the ordinary course of commercial dealing, of an agreement by a company with a subscriber for shares in the company permitting the subscriber to make payments for the shares by instalments" {F-A7}

