-- (8A)(a), (b): "odd-lot" means any amount of shares in the company less than a board lot; "board lot" means a standard unit of trading of the securities exchange
-- on which the company is listed. Two "means" definitions.
-- src:7530 | (8A) For the purposes of subsection (8)(m) —
-- src:7532 | (a) an “odd‑lot” means any amount of shares in the company
-- src:7533 | which is less than the amount of shares constituting a board
-- src:7534 | lot;
@ref s 76(8A)(a) (src:7530-7534)
GIVEN `the number of shares the shareholder holds in the company` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of shares constituting a board lot` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 76(8A)(a) the holding is an odd-lot` MEANS
    IF `the number of shares the shareholder holds in the company` LESS THAN `the number of shares constituting a board lot`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "an 'odd-lot' means any amount of shares in the company which is less than the amount of shares constituting a board lot"

-- src:7536 | (b) a “board lot” means a standard unit of trading of the
-- src:7537 | securities exchange on which the company is listed; and
@ref s 76(8A)(b) (src:7536-7537)
GIVEN `the amount is a standard unit of trading of the securities exchange on which the company is listed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 76(8A)(b) the amount of shares is a board lot` MEANS
    IF `the amount is a standard unit of trading of the securities exchange on which the company is listed`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a 'board lot' means a standard unit of trading of the securities exchange on which the company is listed"

